- **Answer**: ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288 Section 5.7.5 defines fourteen technical processes:
  a) business or mission analysis process;
  b) stakeholder needs and requirements definition process;
  c) system requirements definition process;
  d) system architecture definition process;
  e) design definition process;
  f) system analysis process;
  g) implementation process;
  h) integration process;
  i) verification process;
  j) transition process;
  k) validation process;
  l) operation process;
  m) maintenance process;
  n) disposal process.

- **Reasoning**: Section 5.7.5 of ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288 explicitly lists these technical processes as the actions concerned with technical actions throughout the life cycle that transform stakeholder needs into products or services.

- **Citation**: "The technical processes consist of the following (also see Figure 4 ):
- a) business or mission analysis process;
- b) stakeholder needs and requirements definition process;
- c) system requirements definition process;
- d) system architecture definition process;
- e) design definition process;
- f) system analysis process;
- g) implementation process;
- h) integration process;
- i) verification process;
- j) transition process;
- k) validation process;
- l) operation process;
- m) maintenance process;
- n) disposal process." (ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288, Section 5.7.5, pp. 32–33)

